WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.330
All right, I'm sort of depressed that we have
to do this again, but I'm okay with it and

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:08.570
I'm going to keep doing it until it sticks
and it may never stick and it'll just be an

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:09.570
ongoing conference.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:10.570
[inaudible]

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.030
and if that's the case, then so be it.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:18.710
Bernie Sanders, democratic socialism is not
communism, and in fact, Bernie's democratic

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:20.870
socialism isn't even socialism.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:25.640
It's actually social democracy, which is a
form of well-regulated capitalism, the number

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.859
of emails and is actually going up.

00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:32.140
Then I'm getting about this because Bernie
has a shot at the nomination because more

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:34.510
and more people are paying attention to Bernie
Sanders.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:40.410
The number of emails I get about Bernie communists,
this Bernie socialists, that communism isn't

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.190
invalid.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:43.190
Socialism isn't invalid.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:47.969
There is a lot to discuss and debate and explore
about both, but Bernie Sanders is running

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:50.230
a campaign of social democracy.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:56.030
Now, before we dig into this, I know Bernie
often says he's a democratic socialist.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:57.370
I wish he wouldn't.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:02.430
He may be a democratic socialist, but he is
running as a social Democrat.

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:09.549
This is a type of capitalism common in Northern
Europe and certain other countries.

00:01:09.549 --> 00:01:13.280
Donald Trump calls Bernie a socialist.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.280
Slash.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.280
Communist.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.280
Those are two different things.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:18.020
Bernie is running as neither.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:23.530
Now I tried to do some basic definitions so
that we could at at a basic level, compare

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.590
and contrast the three ideas.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:31.439
There are no perfect definitions because there
will be those who envision a specific type

00:01:31.439 --> 00:01:36.909
of socialism when they say socialism or when
they say communism, they envision some prototypical

00:01:36.909 --> 00:01:38.330
type of communism.

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:43.270
Uh, but I think that this is pretty good as
a starting point for us.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:49.840
Social democracy is a capitalist economy,
strongly oriented towards social justice.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:53.290
And we'll talk more about that in a second.

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:57.780
Socialism is a system of social ownership
of the means of production.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:03.789
And communism is a system of government ownership
of the means of production.

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:07.950
These are not perfect definitions, but this
at least helps us draw some lines.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:13.360
So when you look at this, no matter how you
define this stuff, universal healthcare does

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:16.220
not make a country socialist.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:23.150
Medicare for all is certainly not a, a guarantee
of communism or socialism.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:29.660
Capitalist countries with strong welfare policies
are not socialist and they are not communist.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:33.560
Bernie Sanders does not want to abolish private
property.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:39.770
Bernie Sanders does not want to mandate socializing
ownership of the means of production.

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:45.050
Bernie wants to democratize the workplace
where individual companies are structured

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:47.210
in a more egalitarian way.

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:53.000
Taxation is used to redistribute wealth to
some degree so that no one standard of living

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.080
falls too low.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:03:00.370
This is really pretty uncontroversial stuff
and there's a long list of countries, Denmark,

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:08.800
Sweden, Norway, Finland and others that have
uh, socially democratic, uh, systems similar

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.460
to what Bernie Sanders is proposing.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:17.060
Now there's something very interesting about
social democracy versus socialism of social

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:20.190
Democrats versus actual socialists.

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:27.040
There are strict socialists, actual socialists
that are often very much against social Democrats

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.760
who propose what Bernie Sanders is proposing.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:35.630
Why social democracy makes capitalist countries
more equal?

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:41.450
Social democracy makes capitalist countries
healthier, more viable, better functioning.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:45.020
Social democracy strengthens capitalism.

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:48.180
It takes the edge off of capitalism.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:53.090
Strict socialists are sometimes unwilling
to see things in shades of gray and they get

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:59.440
mad at social Democrats because they say social
democracy will make people more satisfied

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:03.210
with a capitalist system which we want to
go away.

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:08.210
Making it less likely that there will be a
desire for a revolution in which a country

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:10.150
actually becomes a socialist country.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:15.840
Now there are many socialists that are more
pragmatic and they realize we are more likely

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:21.300
to eventually get to socialism from social
democracy than from where we are today.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:25.770
So there are some socialists who from a pragmatic
point of view, welcomed socially democratic

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:26.770
reforms.

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:31.430
Now let's get back to our definitions for
a second just to clarify that even these definitions

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:36.220
are controversial and I understand that there
are some who will say, you know, David, your

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:41.050
definition of social democracy is not really
social democracy, it's welfare capitalism.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.460
And that's something else.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:47.750
Some will say, you know, the real difference
between communism and socialism isn't that

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:52.550
in one the government owns the means of production
and in the other the people own the means

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:53.550
of production.

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:59.680
The real difference is that communism is a
necessarily revolutionary and it includes

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:04.970
a one-party government and one party rule
where a socialism need not necessarily include

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:06.000
those things.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:10.260
So I understand that these are not perfect
definitions, but this is a framework to think

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.810
these things through.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:16.850
But the important takeaway is that by any
reasonable definition, Bernie Sanders is not

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:21.560
running on a communist platform and he's not
even running on a socialist platform.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:27.360
If he is a democratic socialist, then the
platform he is running on is not one.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:32.030
And that is the really important takeaway
that I hope we can all, uh, uh, sort of integrate

00:05:32.030 --> 00:06:32.580
and assimilate into our points

00:06:32.580 --> 00:07:30.050
of view.

